        <mxCell id="9qQqAUZx47hdH7AWglPy-4" value="##Serialization lets Java save a whole object (including its type and all its data) into a file, and load it back later. To allow that, a class must &lt;strong&gt;implement the &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;Serializable&lt;/code&gt; interface&lt;/strong&gt;. It&#39;s a built-in Java interface with no methods. It&#39;s just a marker that says &quot;this class may be saved to a file.&quot;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="300" y="-220" width="530" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
